    array.push(cH, "Paris failed to rescue its social-security budget this morning, and EURUSD's bearish read gained a possible extra step.|No new Bank of England voice today, so cable keeps the pressure tag it earned from Greene and Mann.|Tokyo inflation lands tonight, and USDJPY's watch tag waits to see whether the yen gets a hawkish push.|A holiday Thursday gave the franc nothing to work with, and USDCHF's bullish lean holds.|Brent pushed above $95 for a third straight gain, yet USDCAD's fourteen-point gap is untouched.|OCBC says the bar for another RBA hike is now high, so the Aussie's comeback case against the dollar did not grow today.|New Zealand's official election count is due within hours, and NZDUSD's pressure tag hangs on it.|The French budget committee broke up without a deal, so EURGBP now has a euro-weak scenario next to the pound-strong one.|A failed French committee adds a euro-down scenario to EURJPY's already crowded list.|France's budget setback and a silent SNB leave EURCHF two-sided, with a slight downside tilt.|Both scenarios on EURAUD now point toward the Aussie after France's budget talks failed.|EURNZD loses its small euro lean in the French stress scenario, but stays two-sided either way.|The euro's budget failure and a firmer oil tape both nibble at EURCAD's bullish read.|Sterling heard nothing new and the yen waits for Tokyo CPI, so GBPJPY keeps four scenarios in play.|Two quiet legs on a US holiday keep GBPCHF level, with a pound-side scenario still waiting.|GBPAUD's two scenarios still pull in opposite directions after a day without central-bank news.|GBPNZD drifts at +2 into the kiwi's election count.|Oil's third gain lifts the loonie a little, but GBPCAD's bullish read and its pound upside both survive.|AUDJPY's scenarios still point both ways, and Tokyo CPI overnight may pick a side.|No RBA reaction and no Swiss news keep AUDCHF level, with the Aussie scenario intact.|AUDNZD waits on two answers: an RBA voice and New Zealand's official count.|AUDCAD's bullish read holds even as Brent climbs for a third day.|Two overnight events, Tokyo CPI and New Zealand's official count, could reshape NZDJPY's scenarios.|NZDCHF stays at −2, one step from bearish, with no franc news and the kiwi's count ahead.|The kiwi's count comes first and OPEC+ second, but NZDCAD's bullish read is intact today.|Oil's third rise helps the loonie, but CADJPY's bearish read could still deepen if Tokyo CPI backs Tamura.|A firmer oil price does not threaten CADCHF's bearish read.|Tokyo CPI overnight is the only thing likely to move CHFJPY's quiet stand-off.|Gold steadied above $3,550 after Wednesday's dip below $3,500, but XAUUSD's gold factor did not move.")
