    array.push(cH, "Nothing new from Paris overnight, so EURUSD carries its bearish read and its French-stress upside into Friday.|Cable starts Friday with the same pressure tag, because no MPC member added to or took away from the hawkish case overnight.|Tokyo inflation hit a 16-month high but still missed the forecast, so the yen did not get the hawkish push USDJPY was watching for.|The franc had another empty night, and USDCHF's bullish lean rolls into Friday untouched.|Brent settled higher again, yet USDCAD's fourteen-point gap is the same as last night.|The Aussie's pressure on this bearish call neither grew nor faded overnight: the RBA still has not reacted to hot inflation.|New Zealand's final count left the government one seat short, and NZDUSD's bearish read gets a little deeper.|EURGBP enters Friday with both of its scenarios still leaning toward the pound and no new facts to settle them.|Tokyo's CPI miss takes some heat out of EURJPY's yen-hawk scenario, but the pair stays under watch.|Neither the euro nor the franc had news in the Asian session, so EURCHF stays a flat two-sided pair.|EURAUD's two scenarios both still favour the Aussie side, and nothing overnight changed either one.|The kiwi's lost majority tips EURNZD out of two-sided territory: today's read is +3, a bullish lean.|EURCAD's bullish read is unchanged, but both legs now carry a small threat from the news flow.|The overnight CPI print did not hand the yen a win, so GBPJPY keeps its range of scenarios.|GBPCHF heads into Friday level at zero, with the pound's hawkish scenario still unscored.|GBPAUD's scenarios still point in opposite directions after a silent night for both central banks.|New Zealand's hung result pushes GBPNZD to +3, turning a two-sided pair into a bullish read.|GBPCAD's bullish read survives another oil gain, and the pound's upside scenario is still open.|Tokyo's softer-than-forecast CPI trims the yen side of AUDJPY's scenarios, but the pair stays under watch.|AUDCHF stays level, with its Aussie-side scenario waiting on an RBA voice that still has not come.|The kiwi's election setback lifts AUDNZD to +3, so the cross now leans toward the Aussie.|AUDCAD's bullish read holds into Friday despite Brent's fourth straight gain.|Both overnight events hit NZDJPY: the kiwi lost its majority and the yen missed on inflation.|NZDCHF slips from −2 to −3 after the final count, turning this cross bearish in the shadow.|One of NZDCAD's written warnings came true overnight: special votes removed the government's majority.|Tokyo's CPI miss did not move CADJPY, and the bearish read keeps its deeper yen-hawk scenario.|Oil kept climbing and the franc stayed silent, and CADCHF's bearish read did not move.|Tokyo CPI was the only real news for CHFJPY, and it changed nothing for this haven stand-off.|Gold steadied near $3,565 overnight, but no gold input changed and XAUUSD stays two-sided.")
